## Section: Nouns & Articles

<section id="agreement">
<purpose>How articles and nouns must match in gender, case, and number</purpose>

### Key Insight

<insight title="When uncertain, use the -ν form">
You'll never be wrong if you keep the final ν on τον/την/στον/στην.

<expanded-example label="The simple rule">
For τον/την and στον/στην, you can always include the -ν. Native speakers sometimes drop it, but keeping it is never wrong.

Example: τον φίλο or τη φίλη — both correct!
</expanded-example>
</insight>

### Gender Hints

<gender-hints>
Spot gender by ending:

| Gender | Colour | Common Endings |
|--------|--------|----------------|
| Masculine | ocean (blue) | -ος, -ας, -ης, -ές |
| Feminine | rose (pink) | -η, -α, -ου |
| Neuter | stone (grey) | -ο, -ι, -μα |
</gender-hints>

### Article Quick Lookup

<paradigm title="Article Quick Lookup (ο, η, το, τον, την...)" colour="ocean" defaultOpen="true">

**Singular:**
| Case | Masculine | Feminine | Neuter |
|------|-----------|----------|--------|
| Nom | ο | η | το |
| Acc | τον | την | το |
| Gen | του | της | του |

**Plural:**
| Case | Masculine | Feminine | Neuter |
|------|-----------|----------|--------|
| Nom | οι | οι | τα |
| Acc | τους | τις | τα |
| Gen | των | των | των |
</paradigm>

### Core Pattern

<alert variant="info">
The Core Pattern: In Greek, the article must **agree** with its noun in three ways:
- Gender (masculine/feminine/neuter)
- Case (nominative/accusative/genitive)
- Number (singular/plural)

This is why "the" has so many forms!
</alert>

### Noun Paradigms by Gender

<paradigm-tabs>

<tab id="masculine" count="4">
**Masculine Noun Patterns**

<paradigm pattern="ο -ος" title="Standard masculine" frequency="very common" colour="masculine">
<tip>Most masculine nouns follow this pattern</tip>

**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ος | ο φίλος | the friend (subject) |
| Acc | -ο | τον φίλο | the friend (object) |
| Gen | -ου | του φίλου | of the friend |

**Plural:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -οι | οι φίλοι | the friends |
| Acc | -ους | τους φίλους | the friends |
| Gen | -ων | των φίλων | of the friends |
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="ο -ας" title="Masculine in -ας" frequency="common" colour="masculine">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ας | ο πατέρας | the father |
| Acc | -α | τον πατέρα | the father |
| Gen | -α | του πατέρα | of the father |
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="ο -ης" title="Masculine in -ης" frequency="common" colour="masculine">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ης | ο μαθητής | the student |
| Acc | -ή | τον μαθητή | the student |
| Gen | -ή | του μαθητή | of the student |
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="ο -ές" title="Masculine in -ές" frequency="less common" colour="masculine">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ές | ο καφές | the coffee |
| Acc | -έ | τον καφέ | the coffee |
| Gen | -έ | του καφέ | of the coffee |
</paradigm>

**Vocative changes:** -ος → -ε, -ας → -α, -ης → -η, -ές → -έ
</tab>

<tab id="feminine" count="2">
**Feminine Noun Patterns**

<paradigm pattern="η -η" title="Standard feminine" frequency="very common" colour="feminine">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -η | η αδελφή | the sister |
| Acc | -η | την αδελφή | the sister |
| Gen | -ης | της αδελφής | of the sister |

**Plural:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ες | οι αδελφές | the sisters |
| Acc | -ες | τις αδελφές | the sisters |
| Gen | -ών | των αδελφών | of the sisters |
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="η -α" title="Feminine in -α" frequency="common" colour="feminine">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -α | η θάλασσα | the sea |
| Acc | -α | τη θάλασσα | the sea |
| Gen | -ας | της θάλασσας | of the sea |
</paradigm>
</tab>

<tab id="neuter" count="3">
**Neuter Noun Patterns**

<paradigm pattern="το -ο" title="Standard neuter" frequency="very common" colour="neuter">
<tip>Neuter nominative and accusative are always identical</tip>

**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ο | το βιβλίο | the book |
| Acc | -ο | το βιβλίο | the book |
| Gen | -ου | του βιβλίου | of the book |

**Plural:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -α | τα βιβλία | the books |
| Acc | -α | τα βιβλία | the books |
| Gen | -ων | των βιβλίων | of the books |
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="το -ι" title="Neuter in -ι" frequency="common" colour="neuter">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -ι | το παιδί | the child |
| Acc | -ι | το παιδί | the child |
| Gen | -ιού | του παιδιού | of the child |
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="το -μα" title="Neuter in -μα" frequency="common" colour="neuter">
**Singular:**
| Case | Ending | Example | English |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| Nom | -μα | το όνομα | the name |
| Acc | -μα | το όνομα | the name |
| Gen | -ματος | του ονόματος | of the name |
</paradigm>
</tab>

</paradigm-tabs>

<collapsible title="Common Agreement Mistakes" colour="terracotta">
| Wrong | Correct | Explanation |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| ο καλή φίλος | ο καλός φίλος | Article and adjective must match noun gender |
| τον φίλος | τον φίλο | Accusative drops the -ς |
| η σπίτι | το σπίτι | σπίτι is neuter, not feminine |
</collapsible>
</section>

